{;; The name of the blog, in the navbar and in the title of every page.
 :title            "Bare notes"

 ;; The language of the pages, of the feed and of the Diary calendar, as a language tag such
 ;; as "nl". BareBlog's own words, such as "Archive", stay English. When left out: "en".
 :language         "en"

 ;; How the blog looks: :journal, :notebook, :magazine, :longform or :diary. When left
 ;; out: :journal.
 :template         :journal

 ;; The themes a reader can pick from, by the name of a BareDOM theme preset. The first is
 ;; the one a reader starts with. Every theme: "ocean" "default" "forest" "sunset"
 ;; "neo-brutalist" "aurora" "mono-ai" "warm-mineral". A new blog has all of them: take out
 ;; the ones you do not want. When left out: BareDOM's own look, and nothing to pick.
 :available-themes ["ocean" "forest" "warm-mineral"]

 ;; How many posts a page of the home page shows. Kept small here, so that the example
 ;; has more than one page. When left out: 10.
 :per-page         3

 ;; The line "Powered by BareBlog" at the bottom of every page. Shown unless false.
 :powered-by-footer true

 ;; The logo in the navbar, in place of the title, which it can hold in a font of its own:
 ;; an SVG, PNG, JPEG, GIF or WebP beside this file. One name is the logo in both modes of
 ;; the theme. A map gives one for each, and the one under :dark is shown when the theme is
 ;; dark. When left out: the title.
 :logo {:light "logo.svg" :dark "logo-dark.svg"}

 ;; The icon of the blog in the tab of a browser: an SVG, PNG or ICO beside this file, one
 ;; name or a map as for the logo. When left out: none.
 :favicon {:light "favicon.svg" :dark "favicon-dark.svg"}

 ;; Set these two before you publish.

 ;; Who writes the blog, in its feed. When left out: the title of the blog.
 ;; :author "Your name"

 ;; Where the blog is published, as a full URL. Every link of a published page starts
 ;; there. When left out: the top of the host, which is wrong for a blog on GitHub Pages
 ;; under a repository.
 ;; :address "https://<you>.github.io/<repository>/"

 ;; The picture that a chat shows with a link to a page that has none of its own: a
 ;; PNG, JPEG or GIF beside this file. A square one of 400x400 is shown small beside
 ;; the text, a wide one of 1200x630 beneath it. When left out: no picture.
 ;; :link-preview "link-preview.jpg"
 }
